    {
      "id": 31,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to use this dashboard",
      "datasource": null,
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 66 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Reading the signals\n\n- The **baseline** annotation marks the current 11-container state before any density experiment: per-guest Alloy present, KSM off (`node_ksmd_run=0`), zram at 50%, no limit changes.\n- **Host anonymous** is the main density constraint here; **file cache** is reclaimable and is reduced by shared inodes / consolidation.\n- **KSM saved** only becomes non-zero when `hardware.ksm.enable` is on **and** the workload's pages are marked mergeable (`MemoryKSM=yes` in the guest, or `MADV_MERGEABLE`). `KSM net profit` below zero means KSM is costing memory.\n- **zram saved** is compression gain, not guaranteed free RAM; watch **PSI memory full** and swap page rates for thrash.\n- **btrfs data used** drops when compression/dedup works. Dedup also increases `node_btrfs_used_bytes{block_group_type=\"metadata\"}` until old extents are freed.\n- **PSI panels are empty by design in the baseline.** PSI requires `psi=1` on the host kernel command line; enable it as a separate experiment so its effect is attributable.\n\n## Experiment log\n\n| Change | Watch |\n|---|---|\n| Remove/replace per-guest Alloy | Container anonymous + file cache, host available |\n| Consolidate guests | Per-instance anon/file, host file cache |\n| Enable KSM + `MemoryKSM=yes` | KSM saved/profit, COW/s, CPU, PSI |\n| Raise zram `memoryPercent` / swappiness | zram ratio/saved, swap used, PSI, CPU |\n| Run `duperemove`/`bees` | btrfs data used, metadata used, pool free, IO latency |\n| Share infra or offload monitoring/cache/backup | Container anon total, host anon, host available |\n| Enable `psi=1` on the host | PSI pressure panels |\n\nAdd a Grafana annotation before and after each change so the 24h window makes before/after comparison easy."
      }
    }
  ]
